Manage the IAM groups and their members

Usage:
  nexoctl admin group [flags]
  nexoctl admin group [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Create a group or add members to it
  disable     Disable groups (the policies of a disabled group do not apply)
  enable      Enable groups (the policies of a disabled group do not apply)
  info        Show a group
  list        List the groups
  members     List the members of a group
  remove      Remove members from a group, or the group itself

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for group

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin group [command] --help" for more information about a command.
